{"title":"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/0073ed91e1a9a1cda445af237b7b67815147c979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JKLM$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" /> is drawn with its vertices on the sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4a455d533200d7dfbd00731fa8bd9e8796fb803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bf1e5a1f898db422b11eb7246758290046d9386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PJ = PK = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"14\" /> m, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/8/498d2203eeef25f0a4a2a64d57e8462925343e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JQ = KR = 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" /> m, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddf714d449b9c6ffe450fdbb57763660b3ee8f29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> m, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1e54de87ff17f00d801c9de48ffd0dc0b15494.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR = 66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> m, as shown\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>(put graph on problem 2 page)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine the height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/0/f109bf828aa4b776cf33594caec4d01fd6e11392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PJK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> drawn from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/3926a81a9db71d9566f1f34318868691c7f535b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JK$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b\" title=\"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2b\">part b</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9ea7f9f911c5a1abd87eb3886ca38f58c9730c86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ML = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/3926a81a9db71d9566f1f34318868691c7f535b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JK$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/e/58ed6bb8ec560c108f71ad7fc44cab584c821d04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ML$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> are opposite sides in a rectangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/8/ba8417c664e9b586a2b5c83f9f9198b399d1bd54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JK = ML$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/e/56e8bc23044402bf5314f8ac1bcd5c1d5311d189.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JK = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the point where the height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/0/f109bf828aa4b776cf33594caec4d01fd6e11392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PJK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> drawn from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/3926a81a9db71d9566f1f34318868691c7f535b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JK$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/3926a81a9db71d9566f1f34318868691c7f535b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JK$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/0/f109bf828aa4b776cf33594caec4d01fd6e11392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PJK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is isoceles with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/2/6823d53770a22a3e553efe3e6115c3757b4c94cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PJ = PK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />, we see that the height also bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/3926a81a9db71d9566f1f34318868691c7f535b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JK$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/6/4b6ba02db8e106bd1420592dd6cf5c460debedfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JX = XK = \\frac{JK}{2} = \\frac{6}{2} = 3 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"234\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Next, we can use the Pythagorean theorem to find what <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05fc2c59d25e97ec515446444b44cbe415d3f383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/1/c3100b53bd549c4c51cda882ee3ecb0e383fdf00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX^{2} + JX^{2} = PJ^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/2/6b2a9f1d65c78ad6c61af3d85c3038f084ebe75b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX^{2} + 3^{2} = 5^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8da35ed04d9979f51b96d8999c243e5be24951.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX^{2} + 9 = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/b/08b563836829756c8746a940b50712310be79ac9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX^{2} = 25 - 9 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/a/1cabdcabee41b8ff6aa19769b2a93277c8c9ef57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX = \\sqrt{16} = \\boxed{4 \\text{ m}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"154\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>Alternatively, we could have realized that the sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/a/42a4cb902da448fd99584944a89c1f4f1ae48785.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PXJ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> would have formed a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/1/af1a2cb4ff1720f169ddde1726c1a5a1ab816ae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3-4-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" /> right triangle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05fc2c59d25e97ec515446444b44cbe415d3f383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> would have to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/6437336e9d69072cd98b093bf3e84e7fd626a62a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{4 \\text{ m}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"42\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the point where the height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/0/f109bf828aa4b776cf33594caec4d01fd6e11392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PJK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> drawn froam <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/3926a81a9db71d9566f1f34318868691c7f535b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JK$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/3926a81a9db71d9566f1f34318868691c7f535b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JK$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the point where the height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4a455d533200d7dfbd00731fa8bd9e8796fb803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> drawn from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7c52aff9dd9987076c0ac4fecccf59b6ed8bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7c52aff9dd9987076c0ac4fecccf59b6ed8bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/4/7c4c12988851809387cb21ce44ecdf7774a460df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XKLY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" /> forms a rectangle, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef091d889893c7c10e475a93e4ef626ff70aa5ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> being opposite sides. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/4/a449f0a5f23752e52c9be8fa65edd1af51c0900d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY = KL = 40 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"148\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We can also realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/0/a0080013cb20903a6f4e80fa9450edd707894926.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05fc2c59d25e97ec515446444b44cbe415d3f383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> because of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4a455d533200d7dfbd00731fa8bd9e8796fb803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/0/f109bf828aa4b776cf33594caec4d01fd6e11392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PJK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> (see <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b#Solution_2\" title=\"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2b\">solution 2 of part b</a>) being similar with a scale factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/0/a0080013cb20903a6f4e80fa9450edd707894926.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/c/f3c66d170a701d3a23016cf1be5a36afb1309278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX + XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/4/ca4f4105e7cabed7aff2d14ba2ab17556fa31e29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PY = PX + XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f2539c54a82d7cc4e2a0055322768e77a5c21a37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11PX = PX + 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/c/46c8bc41a2c7ff3743a6287f760c100f11972ae3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40 = 11PX - PX = 10PX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"219\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/7/5b7cf59b6abd8c5f5f10baea3cc4e3fba31c56e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX = \\frac{40}{10} = \\boxed{4 \\text{ m}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"143\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018012744\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.045 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 267/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2059/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10221/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   19.636      1 -total\n 73.97%   14.525      1 2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n 28.54%    5.605      4 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36892:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018012744 and revision id 285649. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}